msgid "**PARAMETER BODY (JSON):**"
msgstr "**PARAMETER BODY (JSON):**"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:536
msgid ""
"**ATTRIBUTES:** A JSON map of arbitrary values to write to the attributes"
" property of the target resource"
msgstr "**ATTRIBUTES:** A JSON map of arbitrary values to write to the attributes property of the target resource"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:540
msgid ""
"This is often useful for storing values from one phase of a Provisioning "
"Workflow for access in another phase. See the video demo below for a "
"complete example."
msgstr "This is often useful for storing values from one phase of a Provisioning Workflow for access in another phase. See the video demo below for a complete example."

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:542
msgid ""
"There are a number of ways that a JSON payload can be statically drafted "
"within a Write Attributes Task or called into the Task as a result from a"
" prior Task. Consider the following examples:"
msgstr "There are a number of ways that a JSON payload peut ser statically drafted within a Write Attributes Tarea or called into the Tarea as a result from a prior Tarea. Consider the following examples:"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:544
msgid ""
"To pass in a static JSON map with static values, use the format shown "
"below."
msgstr "To pass in a static JSON map with static values, use the format shown below."

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:546
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"my_key1\": \"my_value1\",\n"
"  \"my_key2\": \"my_value2\"\n"
"}"
msgstr "{\\n  \\\"my_key1\\\": \\\"my_value1\\\",\\n  \\\"my_key2\\\": \\\"my_value2\\\"\\n}"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:553
msgid ""
"To pass in a static JSON map with dynamic values seeded from prior Task "
"results, ensure the RESULT TYPE value of one or more of the prior Tasks "
"in the Workflow phase is set to \"Single Value\" and refer to the values "
"within the JSON map as shown in the next example. Note that \"taskCode1\""
" and \"taskCode2\" refer to the CODE field value for the Task whose "
"output you wish to reference."
msgstr "To pass in a static JSON map with dynamic values seeded from prior Task results, ensure the RESULT TYPE value of one or more of the prior Tasks in the Workflow phase is set to \"Single Value\" and refer to the values within the JSON map as shown in the next example. Note that \"taskCode1\\ and \"taskCode2\" refer to the CODE field value for the Task whose output you wish to reference."

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:555
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"my_key1\": \"<%=results.taskCode1%>\",\n"
"  \"my_key2\": \"<%=results.taskCode2%>\"\n"
"}"
msgstr "{\\n  \\\"my_key1\\\": \\\"<%=results.taskCode1%>\\\",\\n  \\\"my_key2\\\": \\\"<%=results.taskCode2%>\\\"\\n}"

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:562
msgid ""
"To pass in a dynamic JSON map returned from a prior Task, format your "
"Write Attributes Task as shown in the next example. Ensure that the "
"RESULT TYPE value for the Task returning a JSON map is set to \"JSON\". "
"Note that \"taskCode\" in the example refers to the CODE field value for "
"the Task being referenced. In order for the JSON map to be set correctly "
"and able to be referenced from future Tasks, you must set the "
"\"instances\" key and call the ``encodeAsJSON()`` Groovy method as shown "
"in the example."
msgstr "To pass in a dynamic JSON map returned from a prior Task, format your Write Attributes Task as shown in the next example. Ensure that the RESULT TYPE value for the Task returning a JSON map is set to \"JSON\". Note that \"taskCode\" in the example refers to the CODE field value for the Task being referenced. In order for the JSON map to be set correctly and able to be referenced from future Tasks, you must set the \"instances\" key and call the ``encodeAsJSON()`` Groovy method as shown in the example."

#: ../../library/automation/tasks.rst:564
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"{\n"
"  \"instances\": <%=results.taskCode?.encodeAsJSON()%>\n"
"}"
msgstr "{\\n  \\\"instances\\\": <%=results.taskCode?.encodeAsJSON()%>\\n}"

